  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatDisc_6
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "While attending a research open house at your cancer center, you learn
    that scientists often look at patient data \u2014 like medical records, lab tests,
    or genetic information \u2014 even before any clinical trials start. This makes
    you wonder\u2026\nWhat can patient data tell researchers in the Discovery Stage
    of clinical research?"
  explanation: In this stage, patient data helps researchers understand how a disease
    behaves in real people. By comparing data from many patients, scientists can
    spot patterns in how the disease starts, changes over time, and affects different
    individuals. This helps them focus on the aspects of the disease that matter
    most in everyday life, so new treatments target the problems patients care about.
  correctAnswer: How the disease develops and progresses in different people
  incorrectAnswer1: How safe and effective a new treatment is
  incorrectAnswer2: How many patients will receive the new treatment
  incorrectAnswer3: How patients will respond to a new treatment
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
